TITLE:: SwitchCommand
SUMMARY:: Command that sets each drum step in a row to a hit or a rest.
CATEGORIES:: Commands
RELATED:: Classes/Command, Classes/Parameter, Classes/CommandPrompt, Classes/DrumProgrammer, Classes/DrumStep

DESCRIPTION::
TELETYPE::SwitchCommand:: is a LINK::Classes/Command:: named CODE::switch:: that sets every LINK::Classes/DrumStep:: in the selected drum row. LINK::Classes/DrumProgrammer:: supplies those steps through LINK::Classes/CommandPrompt#-ambientParameters:: as CODE::allNotesInRow::. Empty squares are included.

CODE::values:: is a space-separated list of integers, each CODE::0:: or CODE::1::. Steps are ordered by CODE::startTime:: only. Steps that share a start time take the same value; the list wraps and advances only when the start time changes. CODE::1:: ensures a hit. CODE::0:: clears a hit. This sets the step. It does not flip whatever was already there.

Example: five steps at beats CODE::0, 0.25, 0.5, 0.75, 1:: with CODE::switch values 1 0 0 0:: become hit, rest, rest, rest, hit.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Creates a new TELETYPE::SwitchCommand::. Takes no arguments; the steps are set by LINK::#-execute::.

RETURNS::
A new TELETYPE::SwitchCommand:: instance.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: execute
Applies wrapped CODE::0:: and CODE::1:: values to CODE::\allNotesInRow:: grouped by start time. Each item that responds to CODE::switch_:: is set to that integer.

ARGUMENT:: args
A LINK::Classes/Dictionary:: or LINK::Classes/Event:: with CODE::\allNotesInRow:: (an LINK::Classes/Array:: of steps) and CODE::\values:: (a non-empty LINK::Classes/Array:: of LINK::Classes/Integer::s, each CODE::0:: or CODE::1::).

EXAMPLES::

CODE::
(
var steps = [0, 0.25, 0.5, 0.75, 1].collect({
	|start|
	DrumStep(36, start, GuiPalette.default, 48, 100, 0.0625, { }, { })
});
SwitchCommand.new.execute((
	allNotesInRow: steps,
	values: [1, 0, 0, 0]
));
)
::
